From: GapKeep <noreply@gapkeep.org>
Subject: keymap: Shift with a navigation key that has no shifted entry

The keymaps leave the Shift column empty for PageUp, PageDown, Home,
End, Insert, Delete and the arrows, so Translate() returned KeyNone and
the key was lost. With no shifted entry, such a key is now its unshifted
self; the modifier still reaches the handler (GapKeep: Shift+PageUp and
Shift+PageDown scroll a page). Keypad keys are left alone (Num Lock).

diff --git a/lib/input/keymap.cpp b/lib/input/keymap.cpp
--- a/lib/input/keymap.cpp
+++ b/lib/input/keymap.cpp
@@ -254,6 +254,18 @@
 
 	u16 nLogCode = m_KeyMap[nPhyCode][nTable];
 
+	// gapkeep: Shift with a navigation key that has no shifted entry
+	// (PageUp, PageDown, Home, End, Insert, Delete, the arrows) is that key:
+	// the modifier still reaches the handler, which may use it (Shift+PageUp
+	// scrolls a page)
+	if (   nLogCode == KeyNone
+	    && nTable == K_SHIFTTAB
+	    && KeyInsert <= nLogCodeNorm && nLogCodeNorm <= KeyRight
+	    && !(KEYPAD_FIRST <= nPhyCode && nPhyCode <= KEYPAD_LAST))
+	{
+		nLogCode = nLogCodeNorm;
+	}
+
 	switch (nLogCode)
 	{
 	case KeyCapsLock:
